[{:seon.task/name "a-watchers-end-waits-on-its-own-exit"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the stability sweep of 2026-10-25 (docs/failure-points.md; the owner: platform stability first). Weak: src/seon/watch.clj:58-59 (died) runs .waitFor and slurps stderr on a child that closed stdout but is still alive, and src/seon/watch.clj:90 (stop!) .joins an edge thread that may be parked in on-batch. Correct: the watcher's end is its exit (kill then waitFor, the exit a fact), and the edge thread ends on its stream's EOF, which that kill gives. Proof: a watcher whose child closes stdout and stays alive, and a stop during a parked on-batch, both end."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "a-watch-of-no-existing-root-answers-at-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-26 (root-watches-what-its-loaders-read's review): target/watch over roots none of which exists says no ready: its stream starts from an event id and its ready is fseventsd's HistoryDone sentinel (native/watch.c), which fseventsd never sends for a stream of only missing paths (measured: a watch of one missing dir printed nothing; one existing dir and one missing said ready, and reported the missing one's creation as :root). seon.watch/start! reads that first record with no other answer, so it would wait forever: a wait with no answer, a latent hang. No root meets it today (its docs/ and src/ exist). Correct, at the cause: start! answers at once, typed (:seon.watch/died with why: no root exists), when none of its roots is a directory, instead of starting the watcher; the case of some missing roots is unchanged. Proof red first: start! over two paths that do not exist answers a :seon.watch/died error instead of never answering (a hang on the old code, said in the test's comment)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "a-gone-file-test-means-one-thing-at-one-digest"
  :seon.task/plan "seon.watch-test/a-file-gone-when-its-batch-reads-it-is-a-change is flaky: at one tree (jolt/edit-at-once 65f99d06c2, 2026-10-31) it went red in a plain bin/prove (watch_test.clj:290, \"the page gone when read is recorded as gone\": docs/b.md#b's lead stayed \"It stays.\" where \"It changed.\" was expected, so the other page's change was not loaded when one page of the batch was gone) and green by name, red once and green once more. Its red run's log is kept in runs/evidence/watch-flaky-2026-10-31/ until this is fixed. A flaky test is a defect at its cause (AGENTS §3; task seon.proofs/a-flaky-test-is-a-task): find what the outcome depends on besides the tree (the file's removal against the batch's read, an event order, a directory listing's order, the in-shard neighbours: in the red run it ran in a full shard) and make the test, or seon.watch, mean one thing. Never by a retry or a wait."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.watch-test/a-file-gone-when-its-batch-reads-it-is-a-change}}]
